    "narrative": "The engine room for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is led by **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 85.10. Facing Buehler, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup where his speed profile and favorable platoon alignment are maximized, making him our primary engine for the scarce Stolen Base category. We are also heavily targeting the matchup against Abbott, A, allowing **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, and **Henry Bolte** to project as strong starts (65.39\u201368.90). The combination of a soft pitcher and the elevated lineup positions for **Henry Bolte** and **Max Muncy**\u2014who both see significant upward adjustments for their spots in the order\u2014makes this trio the core of our daily offensive strategy. **Gabriel Moreno** also draws a favorable 66.21 score, buoyed by a strong 0.373 xwOBA, proving that his recent output is more than just a hot streak.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the morning was benching **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 33.54 score. While **Zach McKinstry** has utility value, the elite arm of Miller, B (3.39 xERA) and a bottom-of-the-order placement created a sub-floor situation that forced him to the bench. Conversely, **Austin Riley** occupies a marginal spot at 59.22; while his raw base is high, his position in the 8-hole and a lack of elite matchup conditions temper his ceiling today. We are monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** closely as well; despite his 47.88 score, he faces the formidable Cease, whose elite skill set (2.97 xERA) significantly degrades the efficiency of our OF4 slot. We are playing it safe with our depth, keeping the likes of **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo** in reserve to ensure we maintain optimal efficiency across our game cap while waiting for **James Wood**, **Josh Naylor**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to return to health.",
